// Dev-only type check (D-20 to D-22). Not packaged, never shipped.
//
// This file lives at the repository root, never under extension/, and emits
// nothing: `noEmit` is set, so the compiler only reads source. It runs first
// in `npm run test:recon` (and so in `npm test` and the release candidate's
// automated check), where a type error fails the suite like any test.
//
// The new shared settings module is checked strictly. The accepted v1 files
// join only where they pass unmodified (D-21):
//
//   extension/background.js  checked as shipped, non-strict, by tsconfig.v1.json.
//
// Excluded v1 files, measured 2026-09-28 under this config with strict false
// and nothing changed in the file:
//
//   extension/content.js  1 diagnostic: TS2339 x1 (hasAttribute on the Node
//     type of a MutationRecord target, which the DOM guarantees is an Element
//     for an attributes record). Passing would need an annotation-only byte
//     change, so it stays out until a later phase is already rewriting it.
//   extension/popup.js    8 diagnostics: TS2339 x8 (checked, disabled and
//     indeterminate on the HTMLElement type getElementById returns for the
//     popup's checkbox input). Passing would need annotation-only byte
//     changes, so it stays out until a later phase is already rewriting it.
//
// Neither is a genuine bug: each is a type the checker cannot narrow, not a
// behaviour that goes wrong at run time.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "strict": true,
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM"],
    // Resolved relative to this file, so a scratch config elsewhere that
    // extends it still finds @types/chrome (the non-vacuity proof relies on it).
    "typeRoots": ["./node_modules/@types"],
    "types": ["chrome"],
    "skipLibCheck": true
  },
  "include": ["extension/zhroma-settings.js", "types/zhroma.d.ts"]
}
